          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Work, Energy, and Simple Machines"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.857,
            0.017,
            0.952,
            0.087
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "N 119"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.088,
            0.775,
            0.14
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "when you push a wheelchair, the force applied by you on the wheelchair and its displacement are in the same direction (Fig. 7.7a). Thus, you do positive work on the wheelchair."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.142,
            0.776,
            0.229
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the displacement is in the direction opposite to that of the force, then the work done by the force on the object is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "negative",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". For example, while stopping a ball, the goalkeeper applies a force in a direction opposite to the direction of motion of the football (Fig. 7.7b), and hence, opposite to the displacement. As a result, the goalkeeper does negative work on the ball."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.226,
            0.237,
            0.401,
            0.422
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.226,
                0.237,
                0.401,
                0.422
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.179,
                0.426,
                0.681,
                0.443
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 7.7: Examples of (a) positive, and (b) negative work done on object"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.428,
            0.256,
            0.628,
            0.409
          ],
          "content": [
            {
